@startuml client_send_queue_cancel_activity
title ClientSendQueue - cancelling pending work

start
:CancelPending();
:Lock lifetime_.mutex_;
if (waiting_for_reply_ engaged?) then (yes)
    :Move the callback, reset the slot, and clear its owner;
    :Unlock lifetime_.mutex_;
    if (Callback non-empty?) then (yes)
        :Invoke callback with EPIPE;
    else (no)
        :Discard the empty reservation;
    endif
    :Relock lifetime_.mutex_;
else (no)
    :No pending reply reservation;
endif
while (queue_ non-empty?) is (yes)
    :Move callback from the front command;
    :Remove the command from queue_;
    :Return the command to pool_;
    if (Callback non-empty?) then (yes)
        :Unlock lifetime_.mutex_;
        :Invoke callback with EPIPE;
        :Relock lifetime_.mutex_;
    else (no)
        :No callback to invoke;
    endif
endwhile (no)
:Unlock lifetime_.mutex_ and return;
stop

legend
    The facade has already selected stopping and closed send admission.
    Cancellation never closes the descriptor or publishes stopped.
    A detached active command remains reserved until its transport returns.
    The facade marks lifetime cancellation complete after this method returns.
endlegend

@enduml